ADAPTIVE QUIZ SYSTEM — ORACLE SQL*PLUS FILES

Files:
01_create_tables.sql       Creates the six database tables.
02_insert_sample_data.sql  Adds sample students, subjects and questions.
03_check_tables.sql        Checks tables and sample data.
04_view_previous_attempts.sql
                           Displays previous quiz attempts and results.
05_spool_output.sql        Saves selected SQL*Plus output to a text file.

HOW TO RUN IN SQL*PLUS

1. Extract this folder somewhere convenient, for example:
   D:\25251A05T7\adaptive_quiz_sql_files

2. Open SQL*Plus and connect to your Oracle schema.

3. Run the table creation script (use your actual folder path):
   @D:\25251A05T7\adaptive_quiz_sql_files\01_create_tables.sql

4. Run the sample data script:
   @D:\25251A05T7\adaptive_quiz_sql_files\02_insert_sample_data.sql

5. Check the results:
   @D:\25251A05T7\adaptive_quiz_sql_files\03_check_tables.sql

6. To view quiz history later:
   @D:\25251A05T7\adaptive_quiz_sql_files\04_view_previous_attempts.sql

7. To save output to a text file:
   Ensure D:\25251A05T7 exists, then run:
   @D:\25251A05T7\adaptive_quiz_sql_files\05_spool_output.sql

IMPORTANT:
- Run the scripts using an Oracle schema with permission to create tables.
- These scripts are intended for a fresh set of tables. If you already created
  the tables, do not rerun 01_create_tables.sql; Oracle will report that the
  table name is already used.
- The sample data script is intended to run once. Running it again may create
  duplicate students or subjects; subject_name is UNIQUE, so duplicate subjects
  will cause an error.
- SPOOL output is plain text. Use .txt rather than .doc for SQL*Plus output.
- The Java application still needs Oracle JDBC configuration separately.
